# Ignore rules for the BaraTables plugin repo.
#
# These live here, tracked, rather than only in .git/info/exclude -- that file is local to one
# clone and is never shared, so a fresh clone had NO rules at all. The release command now refuses
# a dirty tree and packages only committed files, while these rules keep local editor/agent state
# out of ordinary development commits.

# --- macOS / Windows / editor noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
.codex/
.serena/

# --- Dependency + build dirs ---
node_modules/

# ANCHORED ON PURPOSE. A bare "vendor/" is unanchored and git matches it at ANY depth, which
# silently swallowed assets/vendor/ -- the bundled DataTables, ECharts and JSZip files
# the plugin enqueues at runtime. Every published GitHub tag through v1.2.1 is missing them and
# is not an installable plugin as a result. This plugin has no build step and no dependency
# manifest, so those files cannot be regenerated: they MUST stay tracked. The leading slash
# limits this to a Composer vendor/ directory at the plugin root, which is all that was intended.
/vendor/

# --- Packaged output ---
*.zip
*.tar.gz

# --- Test + tooling artifacts ---
local-tests/
.phpunit.result.cache
coverage/

# --- Agent instruction files (kept in the parent dev repo, not shipped) ---
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
